---
// ProductDemo: a clearly-labeled, static illustration of the planned Caddie
// workspace. This is NOT a screenshot and NOT a live run — the banner says
// so in plain text. Every "control" is a non-interactive element (span, div,
// list) so keyboard users never land on dead UI, and no runtime fetches or
// client scripts are involved. Numbers shown are illustrative states from
// the planned product (e.g. a plan revision), not results or metrics.
---

<section class="section demo" id="demo" aria-labelledby="demo-title">
  <div class="shell">
    <p class="kicker-inline">Planned workspace</p>
    <h2 id="demo-title">One conversation. Card, tasks and channel in step.</h2>
    <p class="section-lede">
      Work happens in a single project conversation: decisions arrive as cards
      with trade-offs and sources, the task lane tracks what each specialist
      owes, and the channel explains what happened — without exposing raw
      chain-of-thought.
    </p>

    <figure class="demo-window">
      <figcaption class="demo-banner">
        <span class="demo-flag">Illustrative preview — not a live run</span>
        <span class="demo-sub">Static markup of the planned workspace; nothing here is interactive.</span>
      </figcaption>

      <div class="demo-grid">
        <div class="demo-pane demo-pane-card" aria-label="Decision card illustration">
          <div class="pane-head">
            Decision card
            <span class="pane-tag">needs you</span>
          </div>
          <h3>Approve the design boundary</h3>
          <p class="pane-sub">
            Tracker UI · plan revision 3 — approving locks the scope this run
            builds against.
          </p>

          <div class="option">
            <p class="option-name">
              A · React + Hono
              <span class="chip chip-blue">proving first</span>
            </p>
            <p class="option-why">
              The stack being proven end to end, with its acceptance gate
              ahead of it.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="option">
            <p class="option-name">
              B · Flutter + Hono
              <span class="chip">planned</span>
            </p>
            <p class="option-why">
              Mobile coverage from day one, but its stack gate opens later.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card-foot">
            <span class="foot-label">Sources</span>
            <span class="chip">plan · rev 3</span>
            <span class="chip">rules · snapshot</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="demo-pane" aria-label="Task lane illustration">
          <div class="pane-head">Tasks</div>
          <ul class="task-list">
            <li>
              <span class="chip chip-ok">done</span>
              Capture contest rules into evidence
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="chip chip-warn">needs you</span>
              Approve the design boundary
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="chip">queued</span>
              Build the tracker UI
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="chip">queued</span>
              Run browser acceptance
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="demo-pane" aria-label="Channel illustration">
          <div class="pane-head">Channel</div>
          <div class="msg">
            <span class="msg-from">tech-lead</span>
            <p>
              Scope is versioned at revision 3. QA acceptance runs only after
              the boundary is approved.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="msg">
            <span class="msg-from">caddie</span>
            <p>
              Waiting on your approval — nothing gets built until the boundary
              is locked.
            </p>
          </div>
          <p class="pane-note">
            Agent messages will link the evidence behind each claim.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>
